    <string name="norm_info_title">How we calculate your norm</string>
    <string name="norm_info_intro">Water needs are individual, so your daily goal is an estimate based on research.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_base">Base: the European Food Safety Authority (EFSA, 2010) sets adequate water intake for adults at 2.0 L per day for women and 2.5 L per day for men. This is total water, including water from food (about 20%). Because the app tracks only drinks, the base for drinks is taken as 1.6 / 2.0 L.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_personalization">Personalisation:</string>
    <string name="norm_info_weight">• Weight: water needs grow with body mass, so the goal is proportional to your weight.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_gender">• Gender: the base differs between men and women.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_activity">• Activity: physical activity raises water loss through sweat, so a multiplier (1.0-1.5) is applied.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_formula">Formula: goal = weight (kg) x (men 29 / women 27 ml/kg) x activity factor. The value is limited to 1500-4000 ml.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_disclaimer">Important: this is an estimate, not medical advice. Individual needs vary widely. For illness, pregnancy, intense sport or a hot climate, follow your doctor\'s advice. You can adjust the goal manually.</string>
    <string name="norm_info_sources">Sources: EFSA Journal 2010;8(3):1459; IOM/NAM Dietary Reference Intakes for Water 2004; ACSM Position Stand Exercise and Fluid Replacement, MSSE 2007; Armstrong and Johnson, Nutrients 2018.</string>

